    "interconnection": "One travelling carrier crosses two independently controlled track barriers and ultimately serves as the launch wall. An echo left at the first station holds the first rail door open throughout; the middle recoil station redirects a beam into the shared rail/exit signal, releasing the waiting carrier. The final ascent must use that same moving body as both shade and wall.",
    "requiredEvents": [
      "moving-hook",
      "echo-place",
      "plate",
      "held-open",
      "recoil-load",
      "recoil-jump",
      "mirror",
      "stone-lit",
      "gate-open",
      "wallbounce"
    ],
    "solution": "Catch the train from the western ledge and reel in. Near the first low pressure station, release and brake onto its broad plate. Save an echo there, then jump and catch the same train; the echo keeps its first track door open after you leave. At the central signal station, drop onto the recoil plate. Fully load it, release Down and jump as it rises. A little rightward drift brings the rising blade beneath the exposed mirror; cut Up. Its reflected beam enters the sealed receiver and frees the waiting train. Dash Right while holding Grab to chase and recatch it. Reel in through the refill. At the final upper station, pay out and pump gently right, then Updash beside its right edge and hold Jump for the wallbounce. The carrier supplies both the wall and the shade that lets the departure pass the horizontal beam.",
