    "entrance": "Low west boarding ledge, with a long diagonal railway visible ahead.",
    "exit": "High east signal balcony, above the horizontal sunbeam.",
    "nearestExisting": "F19 uses a persistent echo to hold machinery; B40 demonstrates selecting a lifted takeoff; F40 redirects light after departure; F43 makes a transport become a shaded wallbounce face. This superroom gives those operations one continuous causal object: the train first needs a lasting gate weight, then stops at a signal only reachable by leaving its rope, then becomes the launch wall.",
    "novelty": "The signal does not merely open a finish door. It releases the same train the player must immediately chase and later push away from. The first echo remains behind throughout, so the earlier station stays causally relevant across three scrolling views. Three attachments to one carrier and two voluntary station dismounts form one journey.",
    "designNotes": "96×30 tiles, 3.13 normal screen areas. All doors are physical: one pressure gate and one beam/tally gate. The receiver is inside a closed one-tile passage that the body and blade cannot reach from the lower station. The final preview demonstrates the forgiving post-dash wallbounce, while earlier conventional wallbounces remain allowed. The middle station offers a broad spring and separate opportunities to read its signal; the train waits at the signal barrier.",
